    {
      "id": "uTJtQ3T1iPqyZ7fyR1cU3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -519.9965685662755,
      "y": 779.6467010566253,
      "width": 910.0891723632812,
      "height": 1000,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "---XAP-SF2880RjzMATT2",
        "PJK_74p5hBzWcHmiVZMq7",
        "gyw1WUho7UOiQns_cYOla",
        "Zb7KoLEDAvpSTYD33mRIj",
        "41YBo0RqHs4crI1GHUmO_"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ae",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1220964614,
      "version": 4533,
      "versionNonce": 466829530,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790248994049,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Voxtral Mini and Voxtral Small, two multimodal audio chat models. Voxtral is trained to\ncomprehend both spoken audio and text documents.\n\nVoxtral consisting of three components: an audio encoder to process speech inputs, an\nadapter layer to downsample audio embeddings, and a language decoder to reason and\ngenerate text outputs.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAudio Encoder\nThe audio encoder is based on Whisper large-v3. Within the Whisper encoder, the\nspectrogram passes through a convolutional stem that downsamples its temporal resolution\nby a factor of two. The resulting audio embeddings have a frame rate of 50 Hz.\n\nAdapter Layer\nWhisper has a fixed receptive field of 30 seconds. To accommodate audio sequences\nexceeding this duration, they compute the log-Mel spectrogram for the entire audio, but\nrestrict the encoder to independently process each 30 second chunk. The embeddings\ncomputed from each chunk are concatenated at the output stage.\nThe high frame-rate of the audio encoder would result in long sequence-lengths through the\nlanguage decoder. For example, a 30 minute audio at 50Hz has a sequence length of 90k\ntokens.\nTo circumvent this, they append an additional MLP layer at the audio encoder outputs that\nis responsible for downsampling the audio embeddings. A downsampling factor of 4x yields\nthe best trade-off between sequence-length and performance. This results in an effective\nframe-rate of 12.5Hz, enabling Voxtral to gracefully handle audios up to 40 minutes with a\ncontext-length of 32k tokens.\n\nLanguage Decoder\nWe release two variants of Voxtral: Mini and Small. \n    - Voxtral Mini is built on top of Ministral 3B\n    - Voxtral Small leverages the Mistral Small 3.1 24B backbone\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Voxtral Mini and Voxtral Small, two multimodal audio chat models. Voxtral is trained to comprehend both spoken audio and text documents.\n\nVoxtral consisting of three components: an audio encoder to process speech inputs, an adapter layer to downsample audio embeddings, and a language decoder to reason and generate text outputs.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAudio Encoder\nThe audio encoder is based on Whisper large-v3. Within the Whisper encoder, the spectrogram passes through a convolutional stem that downsamples its temporal resolution by a factor of two. The resulting audio embeddings have a frame rate of 50 Hz.\n\nAdapter Layer\nWhisper has a fixed receptive field of 30 seconds. To accommodate audio sequences exceeding this duration, they compute the log-Mel spectrogram for the entire audio, but restrict the encoder to independently process each 30 second chunk. The embeddings computed from each chunk are concatenated at the output stage.\nThe high frame-rate of the audio encoder would result in long sequence-lengths through the language decoder. For example, a 30 minute audio at 50Hz has a sequence length of 90k tokens.\nTo circumvent this, they append an additional MLP layer at the audio encoder outputs that is responsible for downsampling the audio embeddings. A downsampling factor of 4x yields the best trade-off between sequence-length and performance. This results in an effective frame-rate of 12.5Hz, enabling Voxtral to gracefully handle audios up to 40 minutes with a context-length of 32k tokens.\n\nLanguage Decoder\nWe release two variants of Voxtral: Mini and Small. \n    - Voxtral Mini is built on top of Ministral 3B\n    - Voxtral Small leverages the Mistral Small 3.1 24B backbone\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
