      "seed": 1618200390,
      "version": 4785,
      "versionNonce": 206066266,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790248994049,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Multi-task Training Format Framework Motivated by Whisper\n\nThey introduce two special tokens to specify the expected output: <repeat> for repetition\nand <next> for continuation.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThey also develop robust instruction-following behavior, irrespective of whether user inputs\nare in audio or text form. Their speech understanding data falls into two categories: \n    - tasks where audio is provided as context and\n    - the assistant responds to text queries, and tasks where the assistant responds\n        directly to audio inputs.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Multi-task Training Format Framework Motivated by Whisper\n\nThey introduce two special tokens to specify the expected output: <repeat> for repetition and <next> for continuation.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThey also develop robust instruction-following behavior, irrespective of whether user inputs are in audio or text form. Their speech understanding data falls into two categories: \n    - tasks where audio is provided as context and\n    - the assistant responds to text queries, and tasks where the assistant responds\n        directly to audio inputs.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
